{
  "id": "navigation/references/07_enclosing_functions",
  "topic": "navigation",
  "subtopic": "references",
  "title": "Reference enclosing context",
  "summary": "Each reference reaches the editor as a bare location, without the function that encloses it",
  "prose": "clangd attaches the enclosing function through an extension field\n(`containerName`) for a client that declares support for it; clice does not\nread that declaration yet. `clice query references` names the function each\nreference lies in.",
  "status": "unsupported",
  "issues": [
    "clangd#177"
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "int shared_value = 0;\n\nint reader() {\n    return shared_value;\n}\n\nint writer() {\n    shared_value = 1;\n    return shared_value;\n}\n",
      "markers": [
        {
          "name": "variable",
          "begin": 4,
          "end": 4,
          "range": false
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
